precedented rate but  remember lots of homeowners lost their  houses during the crisis so instead of  these gains going to moderate or  middle-income homeowners it's going into  the coffers of huge corporations and  their shareholders and it's all fun  games and easy television for our  glowing surrogates and their newly  remodeled happily ever afters but when  you turn the tv off the reality is a lot  darker one survey referenced in fortune  showed that some 82 percent of  millennials have at least one  significant regret about buying a home  including decreasing home values  neighborhoods that turn out to be a bad  fit and the decidedly unglamorous  realities of fixer-uppers meanwhile  foreclosure spiked a staggering 700 in  january 2022 according to data company  black knight this picture doesn't quite  square with the cheery antics of  christina on the coast so what about the  majority of us left window shopping on  zillow fantasizing about the day we too  will join the ranks of landowners in  some ways we're cosplaying a dream in  stark contrast to reality put  differently we're situating ourselves  squarely within a system  that's rendered us pretty powerless iris  marion young contends that the goal of a  dream house sets workers working and  keeps workers working fearing job loss  working overtime the consumer-driven  desire of civic privatism tends to  produce political quietism that is to  say when we're really worried about  finding our own single-family house  we're gonna work our butts off instead  of questioning the political system that  puts us in this position as sociologist  david madden and urban planner peter  marcuzza write in their book in defense  of housing ownership restricts household  members opportunities to engage in other  activities as well as their desires to  do so especially their willingness to  participate in collective action that  might involve social conflict when we're  more focused on benefiting from a shitty  system we're less likely to agitate  against that system at the same time the  writers argue that this individualist  thinking means that if something goes  wrong the individual is thought to be to  blame rather than social and political  structures the fact that so many  millennials can't buy a house or can't  keep up with their mortgage payments  isn't because they're blowing they're  not keeping up with inflation wages on  avocado toast it's because they're being  priced out by huge corporations zillow's  accessibility belies that reality and  keeps us dreaming and that's what makes  it so seductive but what do you guys  think are you still going to spend your  friday nights on a hot date with the  zillow listings and a rerun of property  brothers or is real estate porn actually  a lot more sinister than the other twins  that do real estate might have you think  let us know in the comments huge thanks  to all our patrons and if you haven't  checked it out in a while check out our  patreon page we have a lot of cool new  stuff there um also check out our new  stream wisecrack live every thursday  right here hit that subscribe button  like you're clicking buy on the zillow  listing for the french riviera castle of  your dreams and don't forget to ring  that bell and as always thanks for  watching later  [Music]  you
 

